    "title": "NSAID use with TDF and hypertension",
    "message": "The patient uses ibuprofen as needed for back pain. Ibuprofen is an NSAID which can impair renal function, especially in the context of dehydration or intercurrent illness. Guidelines highlight that intercurrent illnesses with dehydration may cause renal deterioration in patients on TDF. Concurrent use of TDF, hypertension, and an NSAID increases the risk of acute kidney injury. The plan does not address this interaction or provide safer pain management alternatives.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Advise against regular/prn ibuprofen; recommend non-NSAID analgesics and stress hydration, especially during travel.",
